The <cross product> is $\mathbf a\times\mathbf b=(-2,0,2)$, which is perpendicular to both <vectors>. Any nonzero <scalar multiple> works, so a simple answer is
$$
\boxed{(-1,0,1).}
$$
Its <dot product> with each given <vector> is zero.

