The <gradient> is $(f_x,f_y)=(2-2xy,1-x^2)$. Both <partial derivatives> vanish at $(1,1)$, so it is a <stationary point>.

= b
{parent=3}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The second component of the <gradient> forces $x=\pm1$. The first then requires $xy=1$. Apart from $(1,1)$, the only <stationary point> is
$$
\boxed{(-1,-1).}
$$

