= Solution
{parent=b}

The <divergence> is the sum of the three diagonal <partial derivatives>:
$$
\boxed{\nabla\cdot\mathbf f=-6-6-2=-14.}
$$

= c
{parent=4}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=c}

Each component depends only on its own coordinate, so all cross <partial derivatives> vanish. Therefore the <curl> is
$$
\boxed{\nabla\times\mathbf f=\mathbf0.}
$$
This also follows from the identity that the <curl of a gradient> vanishes for a twice continuously <differentiable> <potential energy>.

