The <matrix product> of the transposed first <vector> with the second is their <dot product>:
$$
\boxed{\mathbf a^T\mathbf b=1\cdot2+3\cdot1=5.}
$$

= b
{parent=5}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The reverse arrangement is an <outer product>, with entries $a_i b_j$:
$$
\boxed{\mathbf a\mathbf b^T=\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\6&3\end{pmatrix}.}
$$

= 6
{parent=Section A}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=6}

The two factors have <moduli> $\sqrt2$ and $2$, and <complex arguments> $\pi/4$ and $\pi/6$. Multiplication multiplies the <moduli> and adds the <complex arguments>, giving
$$
\boxed{|z|=2\sqrt2,\qquad\arg z=\frac{5\pi}{12}\pmod{2\pi}.}
$$
The displayed angle is the <principal argument> in radians; equivalently the argument is $75^\circ$ modulo $360^\circ$.

